          "type": "Boolean"
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "direction": "input",
          "name": "F button name (\"Cancel\")",
          "type": "String",
          "default": "Cancel"
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "direction": "input",
          "name": "T button name (\"OK\")",
          "type": "String",
          "default": "OK"
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "direction": "input",
          "name": "message",
          "type": "String"
        }
      ],
      "python_code": {
        "_body": "_button = live_io.prompt(in_3, [in_2, in_1])",
        "t_button_pressed": "_button == 0"
      },
      "inline": false,
      "live_io": true,
      "note": "Two Button Dialog. idx1=F button, idx2=T button, idx3=message (a corpus caller wires 'No' to idx1, 'Yes' to idx2). The T button is the first button of live_io.prompt; T button? is True when it was chosen. Closing the window answers FALSE (NI): a live_io that shows a window returns the F button's position."
    },
